\[ r = \frac{0.07}{12} \approx 0.005833 \]

Next, calculate \( (1 + r)^n \):
\[ (1 + 0.005833)^{84} \approx 1.586874 \]

Now, plug the values into the formula:
\[ M = 25000 \times \frac{0.005833 \times 1.586874}{1.586874 - 1} \]
\[ M = 25000 \times \frac{0.00925}{0.586874} \]
\[ M = 25000 \times 0.01576 \]
\[ M \approx 394 \]

